## Cairn White

A cairn white is a walking skeleton, rotted and armed with a longsword. It can keep itself unseen until it strikes. Its sword is bound to it and vanishes when it falls.

Wounded, it lets out a funereal dirge. Its blows draw the life out of whoever they land on and leave them drained, and it frightens those it fights. It strikes out one last time as it dies.

One lay hidden in the air by the window of [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Detective Brooks]]'s apartment until [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] cast over the room and found it. It has been destroyed.

## Lovelorn

A lovelorn is small and undead: a knot of wet organs that moves on legs. It hides under whatever is at hand and skitters out to bite, and it holds on after it bites, even to a face, until it is pulled off. Lovelorns frighten the people they fight, and flee when it suits them. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] calls them heart undead.

Two hid in [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Detective Brooks]]'s apartment, one under the couch.

## Pale Lantern Drone

A drone of the [[Org/Pale Lantern Society/index|Pale Lantern Society]] is a skeleton with muscle, sinew and tendon grown over the bones and enchanted to move. At a glance it reads as a person with the skin torn away, and only on a second look does the bone underneath show. It walks and bows, carries what it is given, and does not speak.

One came to the Party's gate at the edge of their fane and stood with one foot over the line, holding an envelope in both bony hands until [[People/Othello|Othello]] took it, then bowed and walked away north.

## Once Was

A once was is a spirit wearing the shape of a person who has died, called by the dead one's own name with once was set before it, as Once Was Thurston. It is barely corporeal, and a blade passes through it almost without meeting anything, though the cut still tells. It can go unseen and watch the living from that hiding, and a dread hangs about it that presses on anyone near. Its touch is cold and hollowing, its stare can fix a mind in place, and void magic mends it in place of harming it. Honest steel barely troubles one; holy light and raw force tell fully, and so does the vigor rung out of a living body.

The three who crewed [[Geography/Hesperid 3|Hesperid 3]], [[People/Ulrich Benda|Ulrich Benda]], Sybil and Thurston, walk its halls as once was.

## Thing from Beyond

A thing from beyond is a skeletal figure wreathed in red flame that gives off no heat. Skin near it crisps and blisters as if sunburned, and it moves without a sound, seldom heeding anything until it decides to. It frightens those it meets, and it is clever: it can fix a person with its gaze, turn a foe's own stroke of luck aside, and touch a mind so that it slows and falters. It is not native to this world, so honest steel finds less of it than it should, and blows of holy light or of raw force carry further.
